  "reproduce_command": "python tools/package_fbhk_followup.py --check",
  "requirements": "Requires the existing BioCoLoop research checkout, its task adapters and scoring code, the authorized CellUMM/Replogle/Nadig and original task datasets, frozen scDEBART weights and compatible model dependencies, locally deployed Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct for controller rollouts, and registered feature/candidate caches. Python dependencies include PyTorch, NumPy, pandas, SciPy, scikit-learn, h5py and the original model libraries. Absolute local paths identify the evaluated run and must be configured in another environment. Source hashes identify dependencies; no raw biological data, predictions, memberships, checkpoints, model weights or credentials are distributed in this supplement. The lab-identity analysis additionally requires the earlier provenance/rebuttal_20261109/experiment_sources.zip (including extensions/rebuttal_20261109/allocation/cpu_runtime.py, allocation_shared.py and run.py) and the full research checkout's extensions/core_ablation_20260922/common.py, extensions/unified_bio_20260918/core_v3.py and task adapters. The earlier source archive alone does not include all these dependencies.",
